  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Nec scutica dignum, horribili</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2">sectere flagello.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Quod magis fuit, cùm ea insitis</l>
    <l n="4">aut officiulis exasperabant.</l>
    <l n="5">Factum Romae, atque alibi.</l>
    <l n="6">Eustathius dici notat : <i>ἀτεφυαλω-τὰς μαςιγας, τὰς ἐξ ἀτεφυάλων</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>σπειρο-μένας καλαχεοτερμένας</i> : <i>Flagra talaria,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>quae talis insertis involutisque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>confecta sunt.</i> Apud Athenaeum</l>
    <l n="10">quispiam recenset, in Parthis</l>
    <l n="11">optimates quoque &amp; Satrapas,</l>
    <l n="12">ubi visum Regi, <i>ψιλθοις ἡ ἱμάσιν ἀτεφυαλωθεὶς</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>μαςιγᾶς</i> : <i>virgis &amp; loris taxillatis cadi.</i> Apuleius</l>
    <l n="14">agnoscit, &amp; <i>Flagrum pecuinis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>ossibus cathenatum,</i> scitè appellat.</l>
    <l n="16">Ille idem Gallis Matrisdeum ad-</l>
    <l n="17">scribit: <i>Arrepto flagro</i>, inquit,</l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>quod semiviris illis proprium gesta-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>men est, contortis taniis lanosi velle-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>ris prolixè fimbriatum, &amp; mul-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>tijugis talis ovium tesellatum, in-didem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" type="foot" para="true">¹ Lib. iv. ² Lib. viii.</l>
  </main_text>
